OSP Remoting NG TCP Transport
Open Service Platform

!!! Introduction

The <*com.appinf.osp.remotingng.tcp*> bundle registers the Remoting NG TCP
transport and, if a listener is configured, exports services over it: every
service registered with the property <[remoting.tcp.enable]> set to true whose
object is a Poco::RemotingNG::RemoteObject is registered with the ORB, and
the URI of the object is stored in the service property <[remoting.tcp.uri]>.
A service that cannot be exported is logged as an error; its registration
succeeds.


!!! Configuring the Bundle

The bundle is configured using the global application configuration file.
The following configuration properties are available:


!! remoting.tcp.listener

The endpoint of the listener, in one of these forms:

  - <host>:<port> for a TCP socket, with an IPv6 address in brackets. With
    port 0, the system chooses a free port, which the URIs of the exported
    services carry.
  - On POSIX systems, an absolute path (starting with "/") for a local (UNIX
    domain) socket. A socket file that exists at the path is removed when the
    bundle starts; any other file at the path is kept, and the bundle does not
    start.

The port is a decimal number. A value in another form, such as a Windows path
or a service name as the port, is rejected, and the bundle does not start.

Without the setting, no listener is created and no service is exported.


!! remoting.tcp.listener.mode

The file mode of a local socket, in octal. Default is 0660: the owner and
the group of the process can connect.

NOTE: The directory of the socket must not be writable by other users. A user
who can write to it can replace the socket file.


!! remoting.tcp.connection.idleTimeout

The time in seconds after which an idle connection is closed. Default is 60.


!! remoting.tcp.connection.handshakeTimeout

The time in seconds for the handshake of a new connection. Default is 8.
